<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.bundle.repacks ~ the pack's collect-the-residency export: a foreign bundle takes the round trip

A multi-tiddler bundle (a `.json` array of tiddlers, or a `.multids`) rides as a PACK: one file, many tiddlers, whose membership rests ASIDE in the bag's `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths`, never on the tiddlers. `REPACK` asks the island to collect the pack's members from that aside map and re-render the bundle through TW5's own serializer, then writes the bytes to disk: the deliberate round trip a foreign bundle takes before an upstream TW5 PR (a `.mem` path recomposes by itself; a foreign pack re-renders on this verb alone).

The pack path derives from the file's mirror-relative address plus its extension, so the source sits under `bags/` or `wikis/`; `out=` names where the bytes land and defaults to the source. REPACK registers as a QUERY verb (read cap, no residency mutation, no effect record), so it asks no `Proceed?` and carries no effect key; only a fresh request id rides each attempt, and a repeat stays safe. Members the bag tombstoned print as missing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ repack-in-place · repack-aside

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`repack-in-place` params=`source/./wikis/lares/bundles/plugin.json from/lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/lares ~ re-render the bundle over itself from the bag's aside provenance`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`repack-aside` params=`source/./wikis/lares/bundles/plugin.json from/lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/lares out/./out/plugin.json ~ land the re-rendered bytes in another file`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ source · from · out · in-wiki · yes

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`source` params=`takes/file needs/required ~ the disk bundle (.json or .multids) whose pack the island collects`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`from` params=`takes/bag-uri needs/required ~ the bag holding the pack's members, whose aside provenance names them`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`out` params=`takes/file ~ where the re-rendered bundle lands; defaults to the source`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`in-wiki` params=`kind/switch ~ run the act in the active wiki's island`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`yes` params=`kind/switch ~ the intent a call off a terminal names in place of the y/N a terminal asks`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

